## 1. Java Learning Big Picture Map

Think of Java mastery as **stacked layers**. Each layer is a prerequisite for the next. Do not skip.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         LAYER 6 — Backend Java (Spring Boot)            │
│   REST APIs · MVC · JPA · Security · Microservices      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         LAYER 5 — Advanced Java                         │
│   Streams · Lambdas · Concurrency · Optional            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         LAYER 4 — DSA in Java                           │
│   Collections · Algorithms · Problem-Solving            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         LAYER 3 — Core Java for Backend                 │
│   Exception Handling · File I/O · Generics · Strings    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         LAYER 2 — Object-Oriented Programming           │
│   Classes · Inheritance · Polymorphism · Abstraction    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         LAYER 1 — Java Fundamentals                     │
│   Syntax · Variables · Loops · Methods · Types          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### How Each Layer Connects to Backend Engineering

| Layer | Backend Relevance |
|-------|------------------|
| **Fundamentals** | Every line of backend code you write uses this. No shortcuts. |
| **OOP** | Spring Boot is built on OOP. Services, models, repositories are all classes. |
| **Core Java** | Exception handling = error responses. Strings = parsing requests. Generics = type-safe APIs. |
| **DSA** | Used in caching, queues, data processing, and every interview round. |
| **Advanced Java** | Streams for data transformation, Lambdas for cleaner code, Concurrency for performance. |
| **Backend Java** | The actual job — REST APIs, databases, authentication, deployment. |

