## 2. Java Learning Phases

---

### Phase 1: Java Fundamentals (Must Have)

> **Depth Level:** `Beginner → Solid`
> **Time Estimate:** 2–3 weeks

#### Topics

- JDK setup, IDE (IntelliJ IDEA recommended), first program
- Data types: `int`, `long`, `double`, `boolean`, `char`, `String`
- Variables, constants (`final`), type casting
- Operators: arithmetic, relational, logical, bitwise
- Control flow: `if/else`, `switch`, ternary
- Loops: `for`, `while`, `do-while`, enhanced `for`
- Arrays: 1D, 2D, iteration
- Methods: parameters, return types, method overloading
- Scope and lifetime of variables
- Basic input/output: `Scanner`, `System.out`

#### Why It Matters

You cannot write a single REST endpoint without this. Every backend function, loop over data, or conditional logic comes from here.

#### Practice Tasks

- [ ] Write a program that validates a user's age input
- [ ] Build a multiplication table generator
- [ ] Write a method that checks if a number is prime
- [ ] Reverse an array without using built-in methods
- [ ] Implement a basic menu-driven console app

#### Mini Project: Calculator CLI

A command-line calculator that handles `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%` with input validation and loop to continue or exit.

---

### Phase 2: Object-Oriented Programming (Very Important)

> **Depth Level:** `Interview + Production`
> **Time Estimate:** 3–4 weeks

#### Topics

- Classes and Objects
- Constructors (default, parameterized, copy)
- `this` keyword
- **Encapsulation** — private fields, getters/setters
- **Inheritance** — `extends`, `super`, method overriding
- **Polymorphism** — compile-time (overloading) vs runtime (overriding)
- **Abstraction** — abstract classes and interfaces
- `static` vs instance members
- Access modifiers: `public`, `private`, `protected`, package-private
- `final` classes and methods
- Inner classes (basic awareness)

#### Why It Matters

Spring Boot's entire architecture is OOP. A `@Service` class is an object. A `@Controller` is an object. You inject one object into another. Without OOP fluency, Spring Boot will feel like magic you don't control.

#### Practice Tasks

- [ ] Model a `BankAccount` class with deposit, withdraw, and balance check
- [ ] Create an inheritance hierarchy: `Animal → Dog, Cat` with polymorphic `speak()`
- [ ] Build a `Shape` interface with `area()` and `perimeter()` — implement for Circle, Rectangle, Triangle
- [ ] Design a `Library` system with `Book`, `Member`, `Loan` classes

#### Mini Project: Student Management System

Console app to add, update, delete, search students. Uses classes, collections, encapsulation, and basic file saving.

