### Collections Framework

| Interface | Implementation | When to Use |
|-----------|---------------|-------------|
| `List` | `ArrayList` | Ordered, duplicates allowed, fast access by index |
| `List` | `LinkedList` | Frequent insertions/deletions in middle |
| `Set` | `HashSet` | Unique items, order doesn't matter |
| `Set` | `LinkedHashSet` | Unique items, insertion order maintained |
| `Set` | `TreeSet` | Unique items, sorted order |
| `Map` | `HashMap` | Key-value pairs, fast lookup (O(1)) |
| `Map` | `LinkedHashMap` | Key-value pairs, insertion order |
| `Map` | `TreeMap` | Key-value pairs, sorted by key |
| `Queue` | `ArrayDeque` | FIFO processing, task queues |

```java
// Most common in backend code
Map<String, User> userCache = new HashMap<>();
List<Product> products = new ArrayList<>();
Set<String> activeTokens = new HashSet<>();
```

---

### Generics

```java
// Without generics — unsafe
List list = new ArrayList();
list.add("hello");
String s = (String) list.get(0); // runtime cast risk

// With generics — type safe
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("hello");
String s = list.get(0); // no cast needed

// Generic method
public <T> ApiResponse<T> success(T data) {
    return new ApiResponse<>("success", data);
}
```

**Backend relevance:** Generic API response wrappers are used in every production REST API.

---

### Strings

```java
// Immutable — every "change" creates a new object
String s = "hello";
s = s.toUpperCase(); // new String, old one unchanged

// Use StringBuilder for concatenation in loops
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
for (String word : words) {
    sb.append(word).append(" ");
}
String result = sb.toString();

// Common operations
"  hello  ".trim()              // "hello"
"hello world".split(" ")       // ["hello", "world"]
"hello".contains("ell")        // true
String.format("Hi %s", name)   // "Hi Alice"
```

**Backend relevance:** JSON parsing, URL manipulation, query building, response formatting — all Strings.

