### Multithreading Basics

```java
// A Spring Boot app handles each HTTP request on a separate thread automatically
// You need to understand threading for:

// 1. Thread-safe singleton
public class TokenBlacklist {
    private static final Set<String> blacklist = Collections.synchronizedSet(new HashSet<>());
    
    public static void add(String token) { blacklist.add(token); }
    public static boolean contains(String token) { return blacklist.contains(token); }
}

// 2. Async operations
@Async
public void sendWelcomeEmail(User user) {
    // runs in a separate thread, doesn't block the request
}

// 3. ExecutorService for parallel tasks
ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
executor.submit(() -> processReport(data));
```

**What to know for backend:** How Spring Boot handles concurrent requests, `@Async` for non-blocking operations, thread-safe collections.

