## 6. Spring Boot Roadmap Preview

---

> This section gives you the map. The deep dive comes after you've completed Phases 1–4.

### What Spring Boot Is

Spring Boot is an opinionated framework built on top of the Spring Framework. It provides:

- Auto-configuration (no XML)
- Embedded server (no separate Tomcat installation)
- Production-ready defaults
- Starter dependencies (one line to add MySQL support, Redis, Security, etc.)

### Core Concepts You'll Learn

#### Dependency Injection

Spring manages object creation. You declare what you need; Spring provides it.

```java
// Spring creates ProductRepository, injects it into ProductService
// You never write: new ProductRepository()
@Service
public class ProductService {
    private final ProductRepository productRepository;
    
    @Autowired  // or constructor injection (preferred)
    public ProductService(ProductRepository productRepository) {
        this.productRepository = productRepository;
    }
}
```

#### The Application Layers

| Annotation | Role | Responsibility |
|-----------|------|---------------|
| `@RestController` | Controller | Handle HTTP, validate input, return response |
| `@Service` | Service | Business logic, orchestration |
| `@Repository` | Repository | Database access |
| `@Entity` | Model | Represent a database table |
| `@Component` | Generic Bean | Utility classes, helpers |

#### REST API Design

```
GET    /api/users          → List all users
GET    /api/users/{id}     → Get user by ID
POST   /api/users          → Create new user
PUT    /api/users/{id}     → Update user completely
PATCH  /api/users/{id}     → Update user partially
DELETE /api/users/{id}     → Delete user
```

#### Validation

```java
public class CreateUserRequest {
    @NotBlank(message = "Name is required")
    private String name;
    
    @Email(message = "Must be a valid email")
    private String email;
    
    @Size(min = 8, message = "Password must be at least 8 characters")
    private String password;
}
```

#### Exception Handling

```java
@ControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    
    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
            .body(new ErrorResponse("NOT_FOUND", ex.getMessage()));
    }
    
    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
        String message = ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors()
            .stream().map(FieldError::getDefaultMessage).collect(Collectors.joining(", "));
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
            .body(new ErrorResponse("VALIDATION_ERROR", message));
    }
}
```

#### Database Integration (JPA/Hibernate)

